United States stock markets staged a robust intraday comeback on Thursday, reversing previous losses driven by a severe tech sell-off. The Dow Jones Industrial Average added more than 550 points as investors rotated out of high-flying technology names and heavily favored consumer and value sectors. Meanwhile, the S&P 500 and the Nasdaq Composite managed to erase earlier deep declines to close marginally higher.
